{% load public_url_tags %}
{% comment %}
The advisory index: filter sidebar beside the results table.

Rendered whole on a normal request and swapped on its own for an HTMX one, so
ticking a facet updates the list and the counts beside it without a page flash.
The facet counts live in this region too, which is why the swap covers the
sidebar rather than only the table.

Everything is a plain GET form underneath: with JavaScript off the noscript
submit button applies the same filters, and the URL is the same either way.
{% endcomment %}
<div id="advisoryBrowse" class="tc-browse">
    <form method="get"
          id="advisoryFilters"
          class="tc-filters"
          role="search"
          hx-get="{% public_url 'core:workspace_advisories_public' workspace_key=workspace.key %}"
          hx-include="#advisorySort"
          hx-target="#advisoryBrowse"
          hx-swap="outerHTML"
          hx-push-url="true"
          hx-trigger="change, input changed delay:350ms from:#advisorySearch">
        {% comment %}
        Search first, on both breakpoints. On a phone, typing a CVE is the fast
        path and should never sit behind a tap; on desktop it reads as the top
        of the panel either way.

        hx-preserve keeps the live input node across the swap, so a search that
        fires mid-word does not steal the cursor back to the start.
        {% endcomment %}
        <div class="tw-data-table-search tc-filter-search-slot"
             id="advisorySearchWrap"
             hx-preserve="true">
            <i class="fas fa-search tw-data-table-search-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <label for="advisorySearch" class="sr-only">Search advisories</label>
            <input id="advisorySearch"
                   type="search"
                   name="search"
                   value="{{ query.search }}"
                   class="tw-data-table-search-input"
                   placeholder="Search advisories...">
        </div>
        {% comment %}
        Narrow screens get a disclosure instead of a wall of checkboxes: five
        severities plus a product per line plus a date range pushed the first
        result most of a screen down.

        It sits directly under the search box, and the source order matches the
        rendered order at both breakpoints, so tabbing through the panel follows
        what is on screen rather than a CSS reordering of it. Hidden on desktop,
        where the panel is always open and there is nothing to toggle.

        The count is the only sign, while collapsed, that the list is narrowed.
        {% endcomment %}
        <label class="tc-filters-toggle" for="tcFiltersOpen">
            <i class="fas fa-sliders" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span>Filters</span>
            {% if query.active_count %}<span class="tc-filters-badge">{{ query.active_count }}</span>{% endif %}
            <i class="fas fa-chevron-down tc-filters-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </label>
        <div class="tc-filters-head">
            <h2 class="tc-filters-title">Filters</h2>
            {% if query.is_filtered %}
                <a class="tc-filters-clear"
                   href="{% public_url 'core:workspace_advisories_public' workspace_key=workspace.key %}"
                   hx-get="{% public_url 'core:workspace_advisories_public' workspace_key=workspace.key %}"
                   hx-target="#advisoryBrowse"
                   hx-swap="outerHTML"
                   hx-push-url="true">Clear all</a>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div id="advisoryFilterBody" class="tc-filters-body">
            <div class="tc-filter-group">
                <h3 class="tc-filter-heading">Severity</h3>
                {% for facet in facets.severity %}
                    <label class="tc-facet {% if not facet.count and not facet.checked %}tc-facet-empty{% endif %}">
                        <input type="checkbox"
                               name="severity"
                               value="{{ facet.value }}"
                               {% if facet.checked %}checked{% endif %}>
                        <span class="tc-facet-dot tc-severity-{{ facet.value }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="tc-facet-label">{{ facet.label }}</span>
                        <span class="tc-facet-count">{{ facet.count }}</span>
                    </label>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
            {% if facets.product %}
                <div class="tc-filter-group">
                    <h3 class="tc-filter-heading">Product</h3>
                    {% for facet in facets.product %}
                        <label class="tc-facet {% if not facet.count and not facet.checked %}tc-facet-empty{% endif %}">
                            <input type="checkbox"
                                   name="product"
                                   value="{{ facet.value }}"
                                   {% if facet.checked %}checked{% endif %}>
                            <span class="tc-facet-label">{{ facet.label }}</span>
                            <span class="tc-facet-count">{{ facet.count }}</span>
                        </label>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="tc-filter-group">
                <h3 class="tc-filter-heading">Published</h3>
                {% comment %}
                    A date range is a plain control, not something the
                    workspace's colour has any say over, so it uses the app's
                    own picker rather than a branded one. See the note in
                    AGENTS.md on which library a trust centre control belongs to.

                    The picker is reached with {% include %} because it is the
                    one component still written as a .html.j2 partial rather
                    than a cotton tag; <c-date-picker> resolves to
                    components/date_picker.html and does not exist.

                    value_binding names an Alpine property the picker reads and
                    writes, so the wrapper below owns that scope. The picker
                    carries no name of its own, so the hidden inputs are what
                    the form actually sends, and their names are the contract
                    the view reads.

                    Setting an input's value from Alpine does not emit a change
                    event, and the form filters on hx-trigger="change", so a
                    watcher dispatches one. $watch rather than x-effect, which
                    also runs on init and would fire a request on every load.
                {% endcomment %}
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-3"
                     x-data="{ from: '{{ query.published_from|date:'Y-m-d' }}', to: '{{ query.published_to|date:'Y-m-d' }}' }"
                     x-init="$watch('from', () => $refs.fromField.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }))); $watch('to', () => $refs.toField.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true })))">
                    {% include 'components/date_picker.html.j2' with value_binding='from' label='From' placeholder='Any date' compact='true' %}
                    <input type="hidden" name="from" x-ref="fromField" :value="from">
                    {% include 'components/date_picker.html.j2' with value_binding='to' label='To' placeholder='Any date' compact='true' %}
                    <input type="hidden" name="to" x-ref="toField" :value="to">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <noscript>
            <button type="submit" class="tc-filter-apply">Apply filters</button>
        </noscript>
    </form>
    <div class="tc-results">
        <div class="tc-results-bar">
            <span class="tc-results-count">
                {% if total %}
                    {{ start_index }}–{{ end_index }} of {{ total }}
                {% else %}
                    No advisories
                {% endif %}
            </span>
            <div class="tc-pager">
                {% if has_prev %}
                    <a class="tc-pager-btn"
                       href="?{{ querystrings.without_page }}page={{ prev_page }}"
                       hx-get="?{{ querystrings.without_page }}page={{ prev_page }}"
                       hx-target="#advisoryBrowse"
                       hx-swap="outerHTML"
                       hx-push-url="true"
                       aria-label="Previous page">
                        <i class="fas fa-chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </a>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="tc-pager-btn tc-pager-btn-off" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fas fa-chevron-left"></i></span>
                {% endif %}
                {% if has_next %}
                    <a class="tc-pager-btn"
                       href="?{{ querystrings.without_page }}page={{ next_page }}"
                       hx-get="?{{ querystrings.without_page }}page={{ next_page }}"
                       hx-target="#advisoryBrowse"
                       hx-swap="outerHTML"
                       hx-push-url="true"
                       aria-label="Next page">
                        <i class="fas fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </a>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="tc-pager-btn tc-pager-btn-off" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fas fa-chevron-right"></i></span>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
            {% comment %}
            The select is only form-associated (it sits in the results column,
            not inside the form), so its change event never bubbles to the form
            and cannot ride the form's hx-trigger. It carries its own HTMX
            attributes and pulls the active filters in with hx-include. The
            form= attribute is what makes the no-JS path work, where it is
            submitted by the noscript button.
            {% endcomment %}
            <label for="advisorySort" class="sr-only">Sort advisories</label>
            <select id="advisorySort"
                    name="sort"
                    form="advisoryFilters"
                    class="tc-sort"
                    hx-get="{% public_url 'core:workspace_advisories_public' workspace_key=workspace.key %}"
                    hx-include="#advisoryFilters"
                    hx-target="#advisoryBrowse"
                    hx-swap="outerHTML"
                    hx-push-url="true"
                    hx-trigger="change">
                {% for option in sort_options %}
                    <option value="{{ option.value }}"
                            {% if option.selected %}selected{% endif %}>{{ option.label }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>
        </div>
        {% if advisories %}
            <div class="tc-table-wrap">
                <table class="tc-adv-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col" class="tc-col-cvss">CVSS</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="tc-col-summary">Summary</th>
                            <th scope="col">Versions</th>
                            <th scope="col">Affected</th>
                            <th scope="col">Unaffected</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="tc-col-date">Published</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="tc-col-date">Updated</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    {% comment %}
                    One <tbody> per advisory: the CVSS, summary and date cells
                    rowspan the product rows beneath them, which is what makes a
                    multi-product advisory read as one entry rather than several
                    unrelated ones.
                    {% endcomment %}
                    {% for advisory in advisories %}
                        <tbody class="tc-adv-group">
                            {% for row in advisory.affected_rows %}
                                <tr>
                                    {% if forloop.first %}
                                        <td class="tc-col-cvss" rowspan="{{ advisory.affected_rows|length }}">
                                            <span class="tc-cvss tc-cvss-{{ advisory.severity|default:'none' }}">{{ advisory.cvss_score|default:"—" }}</span>
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="tc-col-summary" rowspan="{{ advisory.affected_rows|length }}">
                                            <a class="tc-adv-link"
                                               href="{% public_url 'core:advisory_details_public' workspace_key=workspace.key advisory_id=advisory.pk %}">
                                                {% if advisory.cve_ids %}<span class="tc-adv-cve">{{ advisory.cve_ids|join:", " }}</span>{% endif %}
                                                {{ advisory.title }}
                                            </a>
                                            <div class="tc-adv-tags">
                                                <span class="tc-adv-id">{{ advisory.id }}</span>
                                                {% if advisory.is_gated %}
                                                    <span class="tc-lock-chip"
                                                          title="Restricted — shown because you have access to the affected products">
                                                        <i class="fas fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>Restricted
                                                    </span>
                                                {% endif %}
                                                {% if advisory.is_withdrawn %}<span class="tw-badge tw-badge-warning">Withdrawn</span>{% endif %}
                                                {% comment %}
                                                Resolved is the one status worth
                                                seeing without reading, so it is
                                                a badge and the rest stay muted
                                                text. The CVSS chip beside it
                                                still says how bad the issue
                                                was, which is a different
                                                question from whether it is
                                                still open, so the two do not
                                                compete.
                                                {% endcomment %}
                                                {% if advisory.status == 'resolved' %}
                                                    <c-branded.badge tone="success">
                                                    <i class="{{ advisory.status_icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ advisory.status_label }}
                                                    </c-branded.badge>
                                                {% elif advisory.status_label %}
                                                    <span class="tc-adv-status">
                                                        <i class="{{ advisory.status_icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ advisory.status_label }}
                                                    </span>
                                                {% endif %}
                                            </div>
                                            {% if advisory.withheld_product_count %}
                                                <p class="tc-adv-withheld">
                                                    {{ advisory.withheld_product_count }} further product{{ advisory.withheld_product_count|pluralize }} not shown
                                                </p>
                                            {% endif %}
                                        </td>
                                    {% endif %}
                                    <td class="tc-col-product">{{ row.product }}</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-versions">{{ row.affected }}</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-versions">{{ row.unaffected }}</td>
                                    {% if forloop.first %}
                                        <td class="tc-col-date" rowspan="{{ advisory.affected_rows|length }}">{{ advisory.published_display|default:"—" }}</td>
                                        <td class="tc-col-date" rowspan="{{ advisory.affected_rows|length }}">{{ advisory.updated_display|default:"—" }}</td>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </tr>
                            {% empty %}
                                {% comment %}
                                A workspace notice names no products, so it has no
                                version rows — it still belongs in the index, as one
                                row with the version columns empty.
                                {% endcomment %}
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="tc-col-cvss">
                                        <span class="tc-cvss tc-cvss-{{ advisory.severity|default:'none' }}">{{ advisory.cvss_score|default:"—" }}</span>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-summary">
                                        <a class="tc-adv-link"
                                           href="{% public_url 'core:advisory_details_public' workspace_key=workspace.key advisory_id=advisory.pk %}">
                                            {% if advisory.cve_ids %}<span class="tc-adv-cve">{{ advisory.cve_ids|join:", " }}</span>{% endif %}
                                            {{ advisory.title }}
                                        </a>
                                        <div class="tc-adv-tags">
                                            <span class="tc-adv-id">{{ advisory.id }}</span>
                                            {% if advisory.is_gated %}
                                                <span class="tc-lock-chip">
                                                    <i class="fas fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>Restricted
                                                </span>
                                            {% endif %}
                                            {% comment %}
                                            A notice naming no products carries
                                            no status line, so resolved would be
                                            the one state with nothing at all to
                                            show it. The badge is added here for
                                            that alone; the open states read the
                                            same as before.
                                            {% endcomment %}
                                            {% if advisory.status == 'resolved' %}
                                                <c-branded.badge tone="success">
                                                <i class="{{ advisory.status_icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ advisory.status_label }}
                                                </c-branded.badge>
                                            {% endif %}
                                        </div>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-product">—</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-versions">—</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-versions">—</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-date">{{ advisory.published_display|default:"—" }}</td>
                                    <td class="tc-col-date">{{ advisory.updated_display|default:"—" }}</td>
                                </tr>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </tbody>
                    {% endfor %}
                </table>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="tc-empty">
                <i class="fas fa-shield-halved tc-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <p class="tc-empty-title">
                    {% if query.is_filtered %}
                        No advisories match these filters
                    {% else %}
                        No published advisories
                    {% endif %}
                </p>
                <p class="tc-empty-body">
                    {% if query.is_filtered %}
                        Try widening the severity or date range, or clear the filters.
                    {% else %}
                        New disclosures appear here as they are released.
                    {% endif %}
                </p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% include "core/components/trust_center/restricted_notice.html.j2" %}
    </div>
</div>
